{# TEAM · CONFIGURE — how people get in, what happens to an account, and who
   may change either.

   READ-ONLY, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN. Every line here is a fact about the model
   or about who may do what. A control that let one of them be changed would be
   a second place the rule lived. The one list that IS editable has its own
   section, and this page hands over to it rather than inlining it.

   A SCREEN DOES NOT NAME AN ACTION THAT DOES NOT EXIST: there is no row for
   deleting an account and none for a recycle bin, because accounts are
   deactivated, kept and listed.

   THE STRIP ABOVE IS THIS SURFACE'S SECTIONS, written by the shell's frame
   from the sections contract — the same one position a data tab's strip
   occupies. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Team · Configure{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Team/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('team_overview') }}">uhifadhi</a> / team / configure
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Team{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}How people get in, what happens to an account, and who may change either.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    {# ADDING A POSITION — here, and only here (owner 2026-09-22): the
       positions register shows what exists; creation is configuration. #}
    {% if door('positions.configure') %}
    {# ALWAYS OPEN, THE HOUSE CREATE CARD. A position belongs to no department
       and its name is unique across the organization, so there is nothing to
       file it under — the three fields are what a position IS: the name, how
       many may hold it, and the kinds of placement it allows. #}
    <div class="dcadd" id="add">
        <div class="dcaddhd">
            {{ ux_icon('shell:plus', {width: 15, height: 15}) }}
            <b>Add a position</b>
            <span class="hint">The name is unique for the organization</span>
        </div>
        <form class="crcard" method="post" action="{{ path('team_position_create') }}">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrfToken }}">
            <div class="crgrid">
                <div class="crfield grow">
                    <span class="crlab">Name</span>
                    <input type="text" name="name" class="fld" placeholder="Sergeant" aria-label="New position name" required>
                </div>
                <div class="crfield">
                    <span class="crlab">Seats</span>
                    <input type="number" name="seats" class="fld" value="1" min="1" style="width:92px" aria-label="Seats">
                    <span class="zfrag">Blank is unlimited</span>
                </div>
                <button class="cta" type="submit">{{ ux_icon('shell:plus', {width: 15, height: 15}) }} Add position</button>
            </div>
            <div class="crhint">
                {{ ux_icon('shell:info') }}
                <span>There is one <b>Analyst</b>, not one per department &mdash; where each holder works is written on their own record.</span>
            </div>
        </form>
    </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="grid g2">
        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Sign-in<span class="src">&middot; installation policy</span></span>
            <div class="rln"><span>Session length</span><span class="mono d">the installation&rsquo;s own &middot; not held here</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Remember this device</span><span class="mono d">the installation&rsquo;s own &middot; not held here</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Failed attempts</span><span class="mono d">rate-limited per account and per address</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Password minimum</span><span class="mono d">12 characters &middot; no composition rule</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Two-factor</span><span class="mono d">&mdash; &middot; not built</span></div>
            {# "THIS RANGER LEFT IN MARCH" AND "THIS RANGER NEVER EXISTED" are
               different facts, which is why a deactivated account is kept and
               listed. #}
            <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0">Deactivated accounts are refused at sign-in, and stay listed.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Adding somebody<span class="src">&middot; invitation</span></span>
            <div class="rln"><span>Who may add somebody</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span></span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Invitation token</span><span class="mono d">one use &middot; spent when they set a password</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Create with a password</span><span class="mono d">allowed &middot; leaves <span class="mono">invitedAt</span> null, and that null is meaningful</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Reminder</span><span class="mono d">&mdash; &middot; chasing an unused invitation is manual today</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Ranger code</span><span class="mono d">optional &middot; unique where it is given</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2">
        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Accounts<span class="src">&middot; lifecycle</span></span>
            <div class="rln"><span>A deactivated person</span><span class="mono d">stays in every list, keeps their history, is refused at sign-in</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Tier changes</span><span class="mono d">Super Admin and Admin only &middot; a Super Admin cannot demote themselves</span></div>
            <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0">One Super Admin &middot; no second owner, no break-glass.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">Access<span class="src">&middot; permissions</span></span>
            <div class="rln"><span>Who can see Team</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span></span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Who can add and deactivate</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span> &middot; {{ mayAdminister }} of {{ people }} people</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Who can edit the matrix</span><span class="mono d"><span class="mono">team.manage</span></span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Who can station somebody</span><span class="mono d">the area &middot; <span class="mono">assignments.manage</span></span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Who stands above all of it</span><span class="mono d">Super Admin &middot; Admin &mdash; by tier, {{ byTier }} people</span></div>
            <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0">Administering the team is a permission, carried by a position.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="c" style="margin-bottom:20px">
        <span class="tab">Positions vocabulary<span class="src">&middot; its own section</span></span>
        <div class="sxlead">
            <span class="t">{{ ux_icon('shell:file-text', {width: 15, height: 15}) }}<span><b>The words a position is written with.</b> Titles and ranks, not permissions.</span></span>
            <span class="a"><a class="cta" href="{{ path('team_configure_positions') }}">Open Positions vocabulary</a></span>
        </div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Position name</span><span class="mono d">unique inside its department, not across the installation</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Titles offered</span><span class="mono d">{{ titles }} &middot; editable</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Departments a position may belong to</span><span class="mono d">every department on the register &middot; {{ departments }} active</span></div>
        <div class="rln"><span>Seats per position</span><span class="mono d">one &middot; a position with no holder is legal</span></div>
        <div class="use" style="margin-bottom:0">Names only &mdash; what a position may do is the matrix, on Positions.</div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
